 "footnotes": [
  "p. 18 n. 1 (on Àusàr, Pl. IV l. 3): \"In British Museum papyrus No. 9901, the speech of Horus reads :—\" followed by a parallel text in hieroglyphs (3 rows) with transliteration (t'et àn Ḥeru net' tef - f uā menχ en Un-nefer mākuà ḥer bes - nek Àusàr Hu-nefer àu - f sàp mā māχa àu pa teχ hui er àuset-f) and translation: \"Saith Horus the avenger of his father, heir veritable of Un-nefer: I am come to lead to thee Osiris Hu-nefer. He hath been judged in the scales, the weight of the balance resteth (?) upon its place.\"",
  "pp. 17 and 19 (within range): no footnotes."
 ],
 "notes": "p. 17 row 1 continues Pl. III l. 27 from p. 16 (Ani maāχeru). Numeral '29.' is printed between the X1 of Āmemet and its beast determinative; the whole word is kept in l. 28. Plate IV begins under the heading 'PLATE IV.' on p. 17 with numeral 1. Rubric (overline) on p. 17 Pl. IV l. 1 covers t'et, àn, Ḥeru (incl. its stroke), not se/Àuset. On p. 18 l. 5 the overline covers only the I10+D46 group and àn (not Àusàr Ani); that I10+D46 group has no transliteration/gloss printed under it (recorded with empty budge). On p. 18 l. 6 the overline covers t'eṭ - f. p. 18 l. 5: Ani's name has N35 over three strokes in square brackets (restored). 'àn-nà- / nek' (p. 17 l. 1) is split by Budge over two rows; entered as two pieces. Dashed thin vertical lines coded Z1 throughout. p. 18 footnote rule and footnote excluded; p. 19 stops at 'χer Àusàr' above 'PLATE V.'. No hatching/gaps in range."
